## Bilinear PatchMesh, periodic on both axes: nu=4 nv=2, an outer diamond
## ring (radius 0.4) and an inner diamond ring (radius 0.2), each wrapping
## its last strip back to control point 0 -- the case createParametric
## samples all the way to u=1.0 and v=1.0, where a mesh's wraparound
## indexing is most likely to read out of bounds. Same flat, unlit shading
## as patchmesh_bilinear.rib.
##
## A trailing Sphere follows AGENTS.md's "RIB authoring" section, "The
## desync convention."
Display "patchmesh_bilinear_periodic.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.6]
Sides 2
Surface "matte" "Ka" [1] "Kd" [0]
AttributeBegin
	Translate -1 0 0
	PatchMesh "bilinear" 4 "periodic" 2 "periodic" "P" [
		 0.4  0.0 0    0.0  0.4 0   -0.4  0.0 0    0.0 -0.4 0
		 0.2  0.0 0    0.0  0.2 0   -0.2  0.0 0    0.0 -0.2 0
	]
AttributeEnd
AttributeBegin
	Translate 1 0 0
	Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
